      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "In a very weak maiden the first starter ARTEVENTO (4) from the Messara/Gavranich camp gets her chance. By Admire Mars from a Choisir mare whose two foals to race have won, with the talented Gentileschi the pick of them. Improved sharply at her second trial. Won't need to be anything special to give this a shake. DALLAS DUKE (1) has raced twice and been in the money on each occasion, most recently finishing third over 1000m at Coffs Harbour after racing on the pace throughout. Needs to go an extra 250m today but on exposed form he is the pick of the bunch. ZENSEN (3) went keenly last time out at Kembla when stepping up in trip from 1000m to 1400m and consequently dropped out. Worth one more chance coming back a little in trip. MOBILISE (8) lined up for the second time last start and appreciated the step up to 1300m when a close fourth at Kembla. Can play a key role. BECHERS (7) is an All Too Hard half-sister to stakes winner Renewal on debut for Team Hawkes. Betting watch advised.",
